<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/250/150?random=1" alt="Sample Image" style="border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:15px;">
            <h2>Tytuł karty</h2>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu karty.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Tu pojawia się dodatkowa treść po obróceniu karty.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Creates a 3D space so the rotation looks realistic. |
| **2** | `transition` + `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Smooth animation and keeps child elements in 3D. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on both faces | Hides the backside of each face during rotation. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Rotates the back face so it’s facing the viewer after the card turns. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card:hover` | Triggers the flip when hovering. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change direction** – replace `rotateY` with `rotateX` for a vertical flip.
- **Speed** – adjust the `.6s` value in `transition`.
- **Depth** – modify `perspective` (lower values → more dramatic 3D).
- **Content** – swap out the image, text, or add icons/buttons inside either face.

Happy coding! 🎨
